      "body": "## What\n\nThe `(H200 MIG 18GB) Multimodal Processor` shards spend most of their time in CPU-bound Hugging Face processor calls. The container can see every host CPU while it shares the host with the other MIG slices, so each shard sizes its torch/OpenMP thread pools to the whole machine. This sets `OMP_NUM_THREADS=4` on this step only.\n\n## Old\n\n```yaml\n- label: \":nvidia: (H200 MIG 18GB) Multimodal Processor Shard %N\"\n  key: multi-modal-processor\n  parallelism: 4\n  commands:\n    - pytest -v -s models/multimodal/processing/test_tensor_schema.py --num-shards=... --shard-id=...\n```\n\n## New\n\n```yaml\n- label: \":nvidia: (H200 MIG 18GB) Multimodal Processor Shard %N\"\n  key: multi-modal-processor\n  parallelism: 4\n  env:\n    OMP_NUM_THREADS: \"4\"\n  commands:  # unchanged\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Why.** Since the job was sharded 1→4 (#56316), the same 39 cases in one shard vary by more than 3× in pytest time on recent `main`, and the variation tracks how busy the host's CPUs are, not which cases run. The extra time is inside the processor call. During a slow run, one of these shards was a single pytest with ~340 threads using 16–24 cores.\n- **Scope.** A step-level `env:` only reaches this step's containers, through the Docker plugin's `propagate-environment`. No other job is affected. The `mirror.amd` job inherits step `env:` in the generator, so the MI355 mirror gets the same cap and is included in validation.\n- **vLLM respects it.** `vllm/utils/torch_utils.py` leaves an externally set `OMP_NUM_THREADS` alone.\n- **No coverage change.** Same file, same shard flags, same 160 cases.\n\n## Expected runtime and overhead\n\n| Job | pytest | running wall | non-pytest overhead | main overhead cause |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Shard 1–4 (prediction) | runs on busy hosts move toward the uncontended range; uncontended runs roughly unchanged | pytest + ~1–2m | unchanged | image pull / setup |\n\nThis is a prediction, not a measurement: the thread cap has not been timed yet. The validation build will report per-shard pytest time and how busy each shard's host was. If the cap slows shards on uncontended hosts, the value will be adjusted. Aggregate worker-minutes should not go up, because the replica count is unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `yaml.safe_load` on the edited file; the parsed step has `env: {OMP_NUM_THREADS: \"4\"}`, and its mirror inherits it.\n- Scoped validation build with `multi-modal-processor` and `amd-multi-modal-processor`: all shards pass, `OMP_NUM_THREADS=4` visible inside the container, per-shard pytest time compared to recent `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "Thangnguyenvn98"
            },
            "body": "## Validation\n\nBuild [91203](https://buildkite.com/vllm/ci/builds/91203) at `561bc251da` (0 behind `main`), scoped to `multi-modal-processor` and `amd-multi-modal-processor`. All 8 shards passed.\n\n- **Env reached both lanes.** The Buildkite job env shows `OMP_NUM_THREADS=4` on the primary and mirror shards, and it appears on the primary shards' `docker run --env` line.\n- **Coverage unchanged.** 38 + 39 + 45 + 38 = 160 cases per lane, all passed. Every shard logged `HEAD is now at 561bc251da`.\n\n### Primary lane (measured)\n\n| Shard | pytest | running wall | non-pytest overhead | main overhead cause |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 (38 cases) | 14.2m | 15.6m | 1.4m | container start + checkout (unattributed) |\n| 2 (39 cases) | 16.6m | 18.0m | 1.4m | same |\n| 3 (45 cases) | 13.4m | 14.8m | 1.4m | same |\n| 4 (38 cases) | 13.4m | 14.8m | 1.4m | same |\n\n- **Worker-minutes:** 63.2 in total, against a mean of about 71–116 on recent `main`, depending on host load. No extra cost, since the replica count is unchanged.\n- **Slowest shard:** 16.6m of pytest, inside the 20m target.\n- **Against the prediction:** it matches. Shard 2 runs the same 39 cases on every build. Its CPU-bound outlier cases, which took 5–20× longer on contended recent `main` runs, came back to their uncontended times. For example, `allenai/Molmo2-8B` took 30s, compared with 263–474s on slow `main` runs and 25s on fast ones.\n\n### Mirror lane\n\nAll 4 replicas passed. Each one's runtime is in line with its own recent `main` baseline and well inside the timeout, so the inherited cap caused no regression there.\n\n### Caveat\n\nThis is one build. The host was moderately loaded (about 4–5 concurrent jobs), not at its worst. The per-case signature that marked the slow runs is gone, but the p90 effect should be confirmed on `main` over the day after merge.\n",
